DOCUMENT: agent-meta Requirements — Agents Module (REQ-AGENTS-*)
TITLE: Agent Generation and Composition Engine Specifications
VERSION: 0.1.0
CREATED: 2026-05-13
UPDATED: 2026-05-13

[SECTION: Core Compilation + Frontmatter Extraction]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AGENTS-001
TITLE: extract_frontmatter_field() — YAML Frontmatter Field Extraction
STATEMENT: >>>
extract_frontmatter_field(content: str, field: str) → str | None extracts a single YAML
frontmatter field value from agent markdown documents.

FUNCTION SIGNATURE:
  def extract_frontmatter_field(content: str, field: str) -> str | None

INPUT PARAMETERS:
  content (str)
    - Full markdown document with optional YAML frontmatter block (---...---)
    - May contain multi-line field values
    - Required: valid UTF-8

  field (str)
    - YAML field name to extract (e.g., "name", "version", "extends", "patches")
    - Case-sensitive
    - No quotes needed in the field parameter itself

FIELD VALUE MATCHING RULES:
  The function handles THREE YAML value forms:
    1. Unquoted: field: simple_value
       - Regex: ^field:\s*([^\n]+)$
       - Captures value up to newline, trimmed

    2. Double-quoted: field: "value with\n  continuation lines"
       - Regex: ^field:\s+"((?:[^"\\]|\\.|\n  )*)"\s*$
       - Captures multi-line values indented with 2+ spaces
       - Continuation lines joined with single space

    3. Single-quoted: field: 'value'
       - Regex: ^field:\s*'([^']+)'$
       - Captures everything between single quotes

MATCHING PRIORITY:
  1. Try multi-line double-quoted match first (most specific)
  2. Fall back to single-line match (both quoted and unquoted)
  3. Return None if no match found

OUTPUT:
  Returns: str | None
    - Extracted value, trimmed of whitespace
    - Returns None if field not found or value is empty string
    - Multi-line values have \n converted to space (YAML folding semantics)

ERROR HANDLING:
  - No exceptions raised; returns None on parse failure
  - Invalid YAML syntax does NOT cause error; best-effort extraction
  - Empty values ("", '') return None (not empty string)

USE CASES:
  - Reading "version:" for source attribution (REQ-AGENTS-002)
  - Detecting "extends:" field for composition mode (REQ-AGENTS-006)
  - Extracting "patches:" for patch engine (REQ-AGENTS-007)
  - Reading "name:", "description:", "generated-from:" metadata

EDGE CASES & VALIDATION:
  ✓ Field at EOF (no trailing newline)
  ✓ Field with trailing spaces before quote
  ✓ Field value contains escaped quotes (\")
  ✓ Multi-line value with blank continuation lines
  ✗ Multiple same fields → Returns FIRST match only
  ✗ YAML syntax invalid → Does NOT validate, just extracts
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Frontmatter extraction is the foundation for all downstream composition, variable injection,
and metadata tracking. Must be robust to:
  - Both quoted and unquoted YAML values
  - Multi-line YAML strings with proper indentation handling
  - Missing fields (graceful None return, not error)

Used in 5+ contexts:
  1. Detecting composition mode (extends: present?)
  2. Reading base template paths (extends: <path>)
  3. Tracking source versions (version: X.Y.Z)
  4. Reading patch instructions (patches: [...])
  5. Extracting metadata for generated-from attribution
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
Unit tests must cover:
  - Unquoted single-line values
  - Double-quoted multi-line values (2-space continuation)
  - Single-quoted values
  - Empty field (returns None)
  - Missing field (returns None)
  - Field with special chars in value (colons, hyphens, underscores)
  - Field NOT at start of line (should not match)
  - Multiple same fields (first wins)
  - No trailing newline in file
  - YAML syntax errors (invalid quotes, etc.) — best effort extract

Test files:
  - tests/test_agents.py::test_extract_frontmatter_field_*
  - tests/fixtures/agents/sample-*.md (various frontmatter formats)
<<<
