[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AGENTS-002
TITLE: _split_frontmatter() — Separate YAML Block from Body
STATEMENT: >>>
_split_frontmatter(content: str) → tuple[str, str] splits markdown document into
(frontmatter_block, body) where frontmatter_block includes the '---' delimiters.

FUNCTION SIGNATURE:
  def _split_frontmatter(content: str) -> tuple[str, str]

INPUT PARAMETERS:
  content (str)
    - Full markdown document
    - Assumed UTF-8 encoding
    - May be empty or have no frontmatter

FRONTMATTER STRUCTURE:
  Standard YAML frontmatter delimited by '---':
    ---
    name: value
    version: 1.0.0
    ...
    ---
    # Markdown body starts here

SPLIT LOGIC:
  1. If content does NOT start with "---" → return ("", content)
  2. Find closing "---" marker:
     - Search for "\n---" starting from position 3 (skip opening delimiter)
     - If not found → return ("", content) [malformed, treat as body-only]
  3. Split at closing marker:
     - frontmatter_block = content[0 : end + 4]  includes both --- delimiters
     - body = content[end + 4:]                    excludes closing --- line

OUTPUT:
  Returns: (str, str) tuple
    - [0] frontmatter_block: "---\n...fields...\n---"  (empty string if no FM)
    - [1] body: everything after closing "---" (full content if no FM)
    - Guaranteed: frontmatter_block + body != original if FM found (closing --- removed from join)

ERROR HANDLING:
  - No exceptions; always returns 2-tuple
  - Malformed FM (no closing ---) treated as "no frontmatter" → ("", content)
  - Empty document ("") returns ("", "")
  - Document with only "---" returns ("", "---")

USAGE CONTEXT:
  - Preprocessing before YAML parsing (REQ-AGENTS-003)
  - Composition engine base loading (REQ-AGENTS-006)
  - Frontmatter merging (REQ-AGENTS-009)
  - Extension filtering (project-ext.md handling)

EDGE CASES:
  ✓ No frontmatter: "# Heading\nBody" → ("", "# Heading\nBody")
  ✓ Only opening ---: "---\nBody" → ("", "---\nBody")
  ✓ FM without closing ---: "---\nname: value\n# Body" → ("", "---\nname: value\n# Body")
  ✓ Closing --- on same line as body: "---\n---# Text" → ("---\n---", "# Text")
  ✓ Multiple --- in body: FM with 2 blocks → split at FIRST occurrence only
  ✓ Empty FM block: "---\n---\nBody" → ("---\n---", "\nBody")
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Clean separation of frontmatter from body is essential for:
  - YAML parsing without trying to parse markdown body as YAML
  - Preserving exact frontmatter structure for re-serialization
  - Composition engine to apply patches to body only, not FM
  - Extension blocks to know what's metadata vs content
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
Unit tests:
  - test_split_frontmatter_with_fm: "---\nname: x\n---\nBody"
  - test_split_frontmatter_no_fm: "# Heading\nBody"
  - test_split_frontmatter_malformed_closing: "---\nname: x\n# Body"
  - test_split_frontmatter_multiple_dashes_in_body: Body contains "---"
  - test_split_frontmatter_empty_document: ""
  - test_split_frontmatter_empty_fm_block: "---\n---\n"
<<<
