[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AGENTS-007
TITLE: _patch_delete() — Remove Section from Document
STATEMENT: >>>
_patch_delete(content: str, anchor: str, log: SyncLog, source_label: str) → str
removes the entire section identified by anchor heading, including blank lines before it.

FUNCTION SIGNATURE:
  def _patch_delete(content: str, anchor: str, log: SyncLog, source_label: str) -> str

INPUT PARAMETERS:
  content (str)
    - Full markdown document body
  anchor (str)
    - Heading to find and delete (e.g., "## Deprecated Section")
  log (SyncLog)
    - Logging object
  source_label (str)
    - Source file label for logging

DELETION LOGIC:
  1. Split: lines = content.splitlines(keepends=True)
  2. Find bounds: (start_idx, end_idx) = _find_section_bounds(lines, anchor)
  3. If bounds is None:
     - Log warning: "Composition patch 'delete': anchor '<anchor>' not found in <source_label>"
     - Return content unchanged
  4. If bounds found, remove section AND preceding blank line:
     - trim_start = start_idx
     - if trim_start > 0 AND lines[trim_start - 1].strip() == "": trim_start -= 1
     - result_lines = lines[:trim_start] + lines[end_idx:]
  5. Join and return

EXAMPLE:
  Original (lines 0-6):
    0: "# Top\n"
    1: "Intro\n"
    2: "\n"
    3: "## Deprecated\n"
    4: "Old content\n"
    5: "## Next\n"
    6: "New content\n"

  Call: _patch_delete(content, "## Deprecated")

  _find_section_bounds → (3, 5)
  trim_start: lines[2].strip() == "" → trim_start = 2
  result_lines = lines[:2] + lines[5:]

  Output (lines 0-4):
    0: "# Top\n"
    1: "Intro\n"
    2: "## Next\n"
    3: "New content\n"

BLANK LINE CLEANUP:
  - Removes heading line
  - Removes all content up to next same-level heading
  - Also removes ONE blank line BEFORE heading (if present)
  - Prevents "orphaned" blank lines in document

PRECEDENT LOGIC FOR BLANK LINE TRIMMING:
  - Check if line[start_idx - 1] exists
  - Check if that line is blank: .strip() == ""
  - If both true → trim_start = start_idx - 1
  - Otherwise → trim_start = start_idx

ERROR HANDLING:
  - Anchor not found: Warning logged, content unchanged
  - No exceptions raised
  - Safe to call on already-deleted sections (idempotent in effect)

EDGE CASES:
  ✓ Section at start of document: No preceding blank line to trim
  ✓ Section at EOF: Correctly removes to end
  ✓ Multiple blank lines before section: Removes ONLY first blank line
  ✓ No blank line before section: Just removes section
  ✓ Anchor not found: Warning, unchanged
  ✗ Section at start of file with no blank line: Correctly removes heading only

USE CASES:
  - Removing deprecated tools/features from agent template
  - Removing platform-specific sections that don't apply to all platforms
  - Cleaning up agent files after major refactor (remove old approaches)

COMPOSITION INTEGRATION:
  - Part of apply_patch() op == "delete" (REQ-AGENTS-008)
  - Destructive operation (actually removes content)
  - Recommended: Only for removing truly obsolete sections

RISK PROFILE:
  - HIGH: Permanently deletes content
  - Only use when section is confirmed obsolete
  - Version control is the safety net (revert if needed)

SPACING AFTER DELETION:
  - Result should have proper spacing between remaining sections
  - Removing blank line before section prevents double-spacing
  - Multiple deletions in sequence work correctly (each removes one section)
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Delete with blank-line trimming is essential for composition cleanup:
  - Prevents orphaned blank lines when removing sections
  - Enables complete section removal without manual cleanup
  - Supports deprecation workflows (phase out old content gradually)
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
Unit tests:
  - test_patch_delete_middle: Normal deletion
  - test_patch_delete_at_start: First section deletion (no trim)
  - test_patch_delete_at_eof: Last section deletion
  - test_patch_delete_with_preceding_blank: Blank line trimmed
  - test_patch_delete_no_preceding_blank: Heading at start of content
  - test_patch_delete_multiple_blanks: Only first blank trimmed
  - test_patch_delete_anchor_not_found: Missing anchor → warning
  - test_patch_delete_sequential: Multiple delete operations in composition

Integration:
  - Composition engine with multiple delete patches
