[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AGENTS-008
TITLE: apply_patch() — Unified Patch Operation Dispatcher
STATEMENT: >>>
apply_patch(content: str, patch: dict, log: SyncLog, source_label: str) → str
applies a single composition patch (append, append-after, replace, or delete) to document content.

FUNCTION SIGNATURE:
  def apply_patch(content: str, patch: dict, log: SyncLog, source_label: str) -> str

INPUT PARAMETERS:
  content (str)
    - Document (body or full content depending on operation)
  patch (dict)
    - Patch specification with required keys:
      - "op" (str): Operation type (append, append-after, replace, delete)
      - "anchor" (str): Heading anchor for append-after/replace/delete (required for those ops)
      - "content" (str): Patch content for append/append-after/replace (not used for delete)
  log (SyncLog)
    - Logging object
  source_label (str)
    - File name for logging

PATCH DICTIONARY SCHEMA:
  {
    "op": "append" | "append-after" | "replace" | "delete",
    "anchor": str (optional, required for ops other than "append"),
    "content": str (optional, required for ops other than "delete")
  }

  Example patches:
    {"op": "append", "content": "## New Section\nContent"}
    {"op": "append-after", "anchor": "## Tools", "content": "More tools"}
    {"op": "replace", "anchor": "## Deprecated", "content": "## New\nContent"}
    {"op": "delete", "anchor": "## Old"}

OPERATION DISPATCHER:
  1. Extract op, anchor, content from patch dict (default to "" if missing)
  2. Switch on op:

     a) op == "append":
        - Append patch_content to EOF (no anchor needed)
        - content.rstrip("\n") + "\n\n" + patch_content.rstrip("\n") + "\n"
        - Call: content.rstrip("\n") + "\n\n" + patch_content.rstrip("\n") + "\n"

     b) op == "append-after":
        - Delegate: _patch_append_after(content, anchor, patch_content, log, source_label)

     c) op == "replace":
        - Delegate: _patch_replace(content, anchor, patch_content, log, source_label)

     d) op == "delete":
        - Delegate: _patch_delete(content, anchor, log, source_label)

     e) op unknown:
        - Log warning: "Composition: unknown patch op '<op>' in <source_label>"
        - Return content unchanged

RETURN VALUE:
  Returns: str
    - Modified content after patch application
    - Unchanged content if op unknown or operation fails (gracefully)

ERROR HANDLING:
  - Unknown op: Warning logged, content unchanged (not error)
  - Missing required fields: Treated as empty string (delegates handle)
  - No exceptions raised

LOGGING:
  - Unknown op: "Composition: unknown patch op '<op>' in <source_label>"
  - Delegates log their own warnings (anchor not found, etc.)

COMPOSITION SEQUENCE:
  - Used by compose_agent() to apply patches in order
  - Patches applied sequentially: patch1 → patch2 → patch3 → ...
  - Each patch operates on output of previous patch
  - Anchors for later patches must exist in result of earlier patches

EDGE CASES:
  ✓ Empty patch dict: Treated as unknown op → warning
  ✓ op missing: Defaults to "" → unknown → warning
  ✓ anchor/content missing: Treated as "" → delegates handle gracefully
  ✓ Multiple patches same op: Each applied independently
  ✗ Patch order matters: Later patches depend on earlier patch results

USAGE IN COMPOSITION:
  - Part of compose_agent() (REQ-AGENTS-006)
  - Applied to agent body after frontmatter split
  - Patches list can contain multiple operations
  - Order is significant (apply in sequence)
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Unified dispatcher simplifies composition engine:
  - Single entry point for all patch types
  - Graceful handling of unknown operations
  - Logs warnings for debugging composition issues
  - Delegates to specialized functions for correctness
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
Unit tests:
  - test_apply_patch_append: op == "append"
  - test_apply_patch_append_after: op == "append-after"
  - test_apply_patch_replace: op == "replace"
  - test_apply_patch_delete: op == "delete"
  - test_apply_patch_unknown_op: Unknown op → warning
  - test_apply_patch_missing_op: No "op" key → warning
  - test_apply_patch_empty_dict: Empty patch → warning
  - test_apply_patch_sequential: Multiple patches applied in order

Integration:
  - compose_agent() with multiple patches (REQ-AGENTS-006)
